Check whether Minikube is already installed    ------>>>>>> kubectl api-resources ==== to see shortcuts of commands
minikube version

What does this command do?
- If Minikube is installed, it displays the version.
- If it isn't installed, you'll see command not found. That's okay; we'll install it next.

Download Minikube
              curl -LO https://github.com/kubernetes/minikube/releases/latest/download/minikube-linux-amd64

What does it do?
- curl downloads a file from the internet.
- -L follows redirects.
- -O saves the file using its original filename.
- minikube-linux-amd64 is the Minikube executable for 64-bit Intel/AMD Linux systems.

ls -lh minikube-linux-amd64   ----This checks that the downloaded file exists and displays its size

Install Minikube
              sudo install minikube-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/minikube


Verify the installation
           minikube version

You now have two important Kubernetes tools ready:
- kubectl — your tool for communicating with Kubernetes.
- minikube — your tool for creating and managing your local Kubernetes cluster.

— Start Kubernetes using Docker
