                                  Types of services in kubernetes
  1 -- Cluster IP
           It allows us expose our app inside the cluster only. Use for internal communication
           may need to do-->. minikube ssh first  ( to go back to user terminal --->. type exit/then enter)
           curl + cluster IP    to test communication internally
  2 -- NodePort  
           It is used for external communication. It is a type of service used to open communication a static pod e.g worker node
           when you deploy it, it first creates a cluster IP.
           It ranges from 30000 -32767
           To test communication -->> minikube ip , then copy the ip and curl with it together with the target NodePort number
           From the browser use thesame ip+
           Or you can do a Port-farwarding to be able to access the app Kubectl port-fotward (service name) 8080:80, on browser you do localhost:8080:80

  3 -- LoadBalancer
           used to Balance load. when you this it first creates a NodePort, which will create a cluster Ip.
           The challenge of using this is, it is PAID FOR because it has to send a ASYNCHRONUS REQUEST to a cloud provide to provide a loadBalance else it keeps 
           using a NodePort
  4 -- Ingress
           Ingress is most recommented than NodePort because it aggregates services and exposes the app to low port while NodePort exposes the app to high Ports.
           Here the services must be deployed in the cluster. You need to deploy using Helm Chart an Ingress controller inside the cluster which helps handle all the 
           services  within the cluster. It routes traffic to the different backend services. It uses a Role called An INGRESS RESOURCE which is A DEFINITION manifest 
           file to b. it provides SSL termination for security, retries and failures
  5 -- External name
          Here you route traffic without service. It uses and outside DNS resource instaed of an inside resource 


