Kubernetes rollback --  First, let's inspect your Deployment's history without changing anything
         kubectl rollout history deployment/office-web

Inspect revision 2 before doing anything
          kubectl rollout history deployment/office-web --revision=2
          kubectl rollout history deployment/office-web --revision=3

If we roll Kubernetes back to revision 2, Kubernetes will use nginx:latest for the Deployment. But your GitHub YAML will still specify nginx:1.28.
That means a later kubectl apply -f office-web-deployment.yaml could reapply nginx:1.28. In a GitOps workflow, we'd also reconcile the YAML and Git
history when rolling back.

         kubectl rollout undo deployment/office-web --to-revision=2  -- This tells Kubernetes to restore the Pod template from revision 2 
         kubectl rollout status deployment/office-web

         open office-web-deployment.yaml and edit the image back to nginx: latest
