                DATA IN A POD

  Containers running in apod can either be producing or consuming data, or doing both.
configMaps and secrete are k8s volumes managed by k8s while PV,PVC are managed externally

1 - Ephermaral Volume:
      We have diff types based on size, access mode,content that the volume will take.
              - emtyDir: created when a pod is scheduled on a node, the node will create that volume. When the pod is terminated the content of the emtyDir is
                         deleted for ever
              - A hostPath: if the pod is deleted the volume still persist because the volume is craeted on the node where the pod is running
              For remote storage
                      - GcePersistentDist
                      - AWS ElasticBlockStore
              -       - azureDisk
                      - networkfile system

2 - PV 
       This is a volume which provides an APi for users and admin and manage and consume storage
       It can be created by the k8s admin dynamically (using a storage class that provion the volume, mostly used when we have so many pods running) or 
       statistically (manual creation)
3 - PVC
      here pods that are running in cluster look for a volume that has been created either via a storage class or by a cluster admin that match their criteria , 
      when it finds one the user amakes a request and when its granted, its claims it via a pvc

  Pv volumes have diff access mode: (on the node we have a physical file system, while on the pod we have a virtual file system)
      - ReadWrite Once (read-write by a single node)
      - ReadOnlyMany (read-only by many nodes)
      - ReadWriteMany (read-write by many nodes)
      - ReadWriteOncePod (read-write by a single pod)

         Pv and PVC are not managed by K8s

